{"id": "c-mda-revenue", "kind": "filing", "section": "Item 7. MD&A", "text": "Net revenue for fiscal 2025 was $1,842.6 million, an increase of 12.4% compared with $1,639.3 million in fiscal 2024. The increase was driven primarily by higher unit volumes in the Industrial Systems segment and by pricing actions taken in the second quarter, partially offset by unfavorable foreign currency translation of approximately $21.8 million."}
{"id": "c-mda-margin", "kind": "filing", "section": "Item 7. MD&A", "text": "Gross margin was 34.2% in fiscal 2025 compared with 36.0% in fiscal 2024, a decline of 180 basis points. The decline reflects sustained increases in the cost of steel, aluminum and freight, which were only partially recovered through pricing. We do not expect input cost pressure to abate materially in the near term."}
{"id": "c-risk-supply", "kind": "filing", "section": "Item 1A. Risk Factors", "text": "Sustained increases in the cost of raw materials, components and freight have adversely affected our results of operations and are expected to continue to do so. We may be unable to pass these costs on to customers through pricing. Multi-year supply agreements covering approximately 55% of our steel requirements expire during fiscal 2026, and renewal at prevailing market rates would further increase our cost of goods sold."}
{"id": "c-risk-customer", "kind": "filing", "section": "Item 1A. Risk Factors", "text": "We depend on a limited number of customers for a substantial portion of our revenue. Our three largest customers accounted for 41% of net revenue in fiscal 2025, and our single largest customer accounted for 19%. The loss of any of these customers, or a significant reduction in their purchase volumes, would materially harm our business."}
{"id": "c-liquidity", "kind": "filing", "section": "Item 7. MD&A", "text": "As of the end of fiscal 2025 we held cash and cash equivalents of $312.4 million. We maintain a senior secured revolving credit facility with aggregate commitments of $400.0 million, of which $75.0 million was drawn and $9.6 million was reserved for outstanding letters of credit, leaving $315.4 million available. The facility matures in March 2028."}
{"id": "c-segment-industrial", "kind": "filing", "section": "Item 8. Financial Statements", "text": "Industrial Systems segment revenue was $1,104.7 million in fiscal 2025 compared with $958.2 million in fiscal 2024. Segment operating income was $171.3 million, representing an operating margin of 15.5%."}
{"id": "c-segment-aero", "kind": "filing", "section": "Item 8. Financial Statements", "text": "Aerospace Components segment revenue was $737.9 million in fiscal 2025 compared with $681.1 million in fiscal 2024. Segment operating income was $88.5 million, representing an operating margin of 12.0%."}
{"id": "c-headcount", "kind": "filing", "section": "Item 1. Business", "text": "As of the end of fiscal 2025 we employed approximately 6,480 people worldwide, of whom approximately 4,100 were located in the United States. None of our United States employees are represented by a labor union."}
{"id": "c-tax", "kind": "filing", "section": "Item 8. Financial Statements", "text": "Our effective tax rate was 22.6% in fiscal 2025 compared with 24.1% in fiscal 2024. The decrease was primarily attributable to the resolution of a foreign tax examination and to a discrete benefit of $6.2 million recognized in the fourth quarter."}
{"id": "c-legal", "kind": "filing", "section": "Item 3. Legal Proceedings", "text": "In November 2024 a putative class action was filed against the Company in the Northern District of Illinois alleging defects in a discontinued hydraulic actuator product line. We have recorded an accrual of $14.0 million representing our estimate of the probable loss. The range of reasonably possible loss in excess of the amount accrued is up to $30.0 million."}
{"id": "c-call-cfo-margin", "kind": "transcript", "speaker": "CFO", "section": "Prepared remarks", "text": "On margins: look, the pressure we saw on gross margin this year is transitory. We think we have line of sight to recovering most of it through the pricing actions already in the market, and we would expect gross margin to return to something close to prior-year levels as we move through fiscal 2026."}
{"id": "c-call-ceo-demand", "kind": "transcript", "speaker": "CEO", "section": "Prepared remarks", "text": "Demand across our industrial end markets remains healthy. Order intake in the fourth quarter was up 9% year over year and our backlog stands at a record level, which gives us good visibility into the first half of next year."}
{"id": "c-call-cfo-guidance", "kind": "transcript", "speaker": "CFO", "section": "Prepared remarks", "text": "Turning to guidance. For fiscal 2026 we expect revenue growth of 6 to 8 percent, adjusted operating margin of 13.5 to 14.0 percent, and free cash flow conversion above 90 percent of adjusted net income."}
{"id": "c-call-qa-pricing", "kind": "transcript", "speaker": "analyst", "section": "Q&A", "text": "Analyst: Can you talk about how much of the pricing you put through in the second quarter is actually sticking with customers, and whether you are seeing any pushback on renewals given where steel is trading?"}
{"id": "c-call-qa-cfo-answer", "kind": "transcript", "speaker": "CFO", "section": "Q&A", "text": "CFO: Roughly three quarters of the announced pricing is holding. There is some pushback in the longer-dated industrial contracts, and I would say the renewal conversations are harder than they were a year ago, but nothing that changes our view of the full year."}
